-NEVER WRITE ANOTHER ROLE'S ATTESTATION FIELD. Some fields are OUTPUTS of a step you are not performing, and writing one forges the evidence that a gate reads. The canonical case is `- Readiness:` (`go`/`go-pending-approval`/`no-go`), which is an output of `/plan-review`: the auto-approve predicate reads that FIELD FIRST and only falls back to parsing the workflow history when it is ABSENT, so a hand-written value asserts that a review cleared the plan, and under `--full-auto` that assertion is what promotes a plan to approved and its queue action to `execute`. Measured 2026-09-06: an agent authoring a four-plan Set wrote `Readiness: go-pending-approval` into all four having run no review, and the predicate returned True for every one. So when AUTHORING, OMIT the field: absence is the correct state, it is silent, and it makes the gate fail closed. `aw ipd scaffold` already omits it; do not add it. `aw ipd lint` refuses an unattested value (`IPD-M107`), which also blocks `aw ipd begin`. The same rule generalizes: never hand-write an `- Approval:` attestation, a `V-*` `Observed evidence` block you did not observe, or an `Execution state: performed` for work you did not do.
+NEVER WRITE ANOTHER ROLE'S ATTESTATION. Some metadata fields are OUTPUTS of a step you are not performing, and hand-editing a metadata log or front-matter mirror forges the evidence that a gate reads. The canonical case is review readiness (`go`/`go-pending-approval`/`no-go`), which is an output of `/plan-review` recorded as a `review` event in the plan's metadata log by `aw reviews record` (never by hand). Under the legacy bullet format (measured 2026-09-06), an agent authoring a four-plan Set wrote `Readiness: go-pending-approval` into all four having run no review, and the auto-approve predicate returned True for every one. When AUTHORING, never write readiness or hand-edit `.aw/records/meta/<id6>.jsonl`: absence of a review event is the correct state, it is silent, and it makes the gate fail closed. `aw ipd scaffold` creates a conformant skeleton and metadata log with no review event; `aw check meta` and `aw ipd lint` fail closed on unattested or tampered metadata (repair drift only with `aw meta repair <id6>`). The same rule generalizes: never forge an approval attestation (recorded only via `aw ipd set approved <id6> --by-human`), a `V-*` `Observed evidence` block you did not observe, or an `Execution state: performed` for work you did not do.
 
 AN ORCHESTRATOR HOLDS ORCHESTRATION, NOT WORK OF ITS OWN, AND THE DISTINCTION IS NOT 'has no checklist'. An Order-0 orchestrator SHOULD carry a checklist of its children: that checklist is what makes a Set execute completely and in order when a human simply tells an agent 'execute <setid>' with no runner involved, which is how most Sets are run. DELETING it causes exactly the lost or partial work it exists to prevent. What must NOT be there is work that exists ONLY on the parent and is covered by no child: producing a deliverable, establishing a baseline before any child runs, reconciling records afterwards. The reason is mechanical: the runner RETIRES an orchestrator once every child is `executed` and deliberately SKIPS the pre-transition E/V checkpoint, on the premise that the parent's items are performed by nobody. Work parked on the parent is therefore marked complete having never been performed OR verified. So if you are authoring a Set and find yourself writing a STEP on the Order-0 plan that no child covers, do NOT delete it: ADD A CHILD for it. EVERY plan carrying `- Kind: orchestrator` carries checklist items, without exception, and most of those items are legitimate orchestration, which is why the distinction matters and why a blunt 'no items on a parent' rule is wrong. That is stated as a PROPERTY rather than as a fraction because the fraction rotted three times: it read '46 of 130', whose denominator was the filename `-00-` population, most of which are pre-`Kind` legacy plans carrying ZERO E-items and so diluting a ratio they are not members of; measured on the plans that actually declare the kind it has been 100 percent at every single measurement. AND A RUN NOW CHECKS THIS RATHER THAN TRUSTING YOU TO: see the ORCHESTRATOR COVERAGE GATE described under 'The runners own ordering, isolation, and orchestrators' above, which refuses before spending anything and tells you to add a child.
 
